//! Panic-injection fuzzing, oracle V1/V2, a harness false positive. A
//! Transient OneForAll child stopped itself with `Shutdown` while a keyed
//! blocking job held armed payloads (a scheduled emit, the result, `done`).
//! Their destructors panicked during its cleanup, recorded as its cleanup
//! failure, and a Transient child restarts on a cleanup failure (L6): the
//! supervisor was right. The restart oracles now take the recorded
//! `cleanup_failure()` as ground truth, since such a payload can go off on
//! another task (the deadline service) than the actor's.
//!
//! Generated by `cargo run --example repro -- <input> --emit transient_restarts_on_job_payload_cleanup`.
//!
//! Failure: none (passing input)
//! Strategy random, seed 142514507397206.
